 "title": "Two classes of knots and the global hollow triples",
 "status": "Partial",
 "claim": "If the knots of a finite pattern split into two classes, every co-knotted pair in exactly one knot of each, the two classes and their union have the same NAE states; so each knot of one class is forced by the other. Registered: OVERLAP-READ's global hollow triples are knots the swaps removed (G1), forced by the untouched class when the removed knots lie in one class (G2).",
